WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.580
Hey, it's Patrick coming to you from Vancouver on this Friday

00:00:02.580 --> 00:00:05.620
edition of Tesla Short's Time Daily episode 439.

00:00:05.620 --> 00:00:07.440
It's April 17th, 2026.

00:00:07.620 --> 00:00:09.880
Let's sit down for a few minutes and catch you up on what

00:00:09.880 --> 00:00:12.760
actually moved the needle this week before we head into the weekend.

00:00:13.280 --> 00:00:16.540
There's a nice mix of near-term progress, long-term vision stuff,

00:00:16.680 --> 00:00:18.900
and some honest reality checks in the mix today.

00:00:19.440 --> 00:00:21.280
Here's what's making news in the Tesla world.

00:00:21.820 --> 00:00:25.380
First up, Tesla didn't sit around after finally getting full self-driving

00:00:25.380 --> 00:00:27.300
supervised approved in the Netherlands.

00:00:27.860 --> 00:00:31.100
Within a week, they were already pushing out free trials to local owners.

00:00:31.660 --> 00:00:33.180
The goal is pretty straightforward.

00:00:33.600 --> 00:00:36.900
They want real European drivers putting miles on the system,

00:00:37.080 --> 00:00:40.140
so the team can gather feedback specific to those narrower roads,

00:00:40.420 --> 00:00:43.620
different signage, and the way traffic actually flows over there.

00:00:43.840 --> 00:00:47.260
It's also a smart way to build some genuine excitement and familiarity

00:00:47.780 --> 00:00:50.440
before the feature eventually flips over to paid.

00:00:51.100 --> 00:00:54.000
From a business standpoint, this feels like a pragmatic move

00:00:54.000 --> 00:00:56.940
to start cracking a market that has been waiting quite a while

00:00:56.940 --> 00:00:58.980
for meaningful autonomy progress.

00:00:59.880 --> 00:01:01.580
Regulatory approval is one thing,

00:01:01.760 --> 00:01:05.940
but turning that approval into actual usage and usable data

00:01:05.940 --> 00:01:07.320
is what really matters next.

00:01:07.800 --> 00:01:11.640
This shows Tesla adapting their rollout strategy to local realities

00:01:11.640 --> 00:01:14.620
rather than forcing one-size-fits-all approach

00:01:14.620 --> 00:01:16.500
they've sometimes been accused of in the past.

00:01:17.360 --> 00:01:19.980
Europe has always been a bit of a tougher nut for them

00:01:19.980 --> 00:01:23.300
on the regulatory side, so seeing them move quickly

00:01:23.300 --> 00:01:26.320
once the door cracked open feels like a mature evolution

00:01:26.320 --> 00:01:28.940
in how they bring features to different continents.

00:01:29.380 --> 00:01:32.100
I'm curious to see what kind of unique edge cases

00:01:32.100 --> 00:01:36.160
the Dutch owners surface that maybe California or Texas drives don't.

00:01:36.440 --> 00:01:38.300
While that autonomy news is exciting,

00:01:38.780 --> 00:01:40.600
a lot of owners are getting some more immediate,

00:01:40.800 --> 00:01:43.260
tangible improvements through the latest software drop.

00:01:43.520 --> 00:01:48.060
The 2026.14.1 update just had its release notes published,

00:01:48.340 --> 00:01:50.840
and it's one of those classic Tesla packages

00:01:50.840 --> 00:01:55.060
that quietly makes the car feel noticeably better in day-to-day life.

00:01:55.480 --> 00:01:57.360
It brings a new self-driving app,

00:01:57.560 --> 00:02:01.240
hey, Grock voice activation, upgrades to the immersive sound system,

00:02:01.740 --> 00:02:03.360
meaningful improvements to pet mode,

00:02:03.640 --> 00:02:06.380
and those blind spot warning lights that now illuminate

00:02:06.380 --> 00:02:08.220
right on the mirrors instead of just the screen.

00:02:08.900 --> 00:02:10.400
Music queuing is smarter now,

00:02:10.540 --> 00:02:12.440
and there's even a new sketchpad feature added

00:02:12.440 --> 00:02:15.380
for whoever wants to doodle on the big screen while waiting somewhere.

00:02:16.080 --> 00:02:18.460
None of these changes are revolutionary on their own.

00:02:18.460 --> 00:02:20.140
Yet when you put them all together,

00:02:20.340 --> 00:02:22.680
they reinforce how Tesla keeps treating the car

00:02:22.680 --> 00:02:26.200
like a device that can feel fresher and more capable over time

00:02:26.200 --> 00:02:27.640
through over-the-air updates.

00:02:28.100 --> 00:02:31.320
Owners continue to see their existing vehicles gain new capabilities

00:02:31.320 --> 00:02:32.940
without having to buy anything new.

00:02:33.300 --> 00:02:37.240
That steady stream of polish really adds to the long-term product experience

00:02:37.240 --> 00:02:39.440
and helps justify the upfront investment

00:02:39.440 --> 00:02:42.580
for a lot of people who wonder if they're paying a premium today

00:02:42.580 --> 00:02:44.920
for tech that will keep paying them back for years.

00:02:45.560 --> 00:02:48.380
What strikes me is how this approach still sets them apart.

00:02:49.100 --> 00:02:53.460
While other manufacturers tend to tie new features to the next model year

00:02:53.460 --> 00:02:55.300
or a paid hardware upgrade,

00:02:55.880 --> 00:02:58.320
Tesla's willingness to keep refreshing older cars

00:02:58.320 --> 00:02:59.900
builds a different kind of loyalty.

00:03:00.420 --> 00:03:03.120
It turns the vehicle into something closer to a phone

00:03:03.120 --> 00:03:04.860
that gets better instead of a appliance

00:03:04.860 --> 00:03:06.260
that slowly gets outdated.

00:03:06.760 --> 00:03:09.400
That constant polishing is part of the bigger picture

00:03:09.400 --> 00:03:12.560
Tesla painted in a new teaser video that dropped this week.

00:03:12.560 --> 00:03:16.400
The video positions right now as the golden era of transportation.

00:03:16.680 --> 00:03:20.100
It focuses heavily on robotaxies, the cybercab,

00:03:20.320 --> 00:03:23.760
and the longer-term possibility of gradually shifting away

00:03:23.760 --> 00:03:26.180
from traditional car ownership for a lot of people.

00:03:26.580 --> 00:03:28.780
The tone is classic ambitious Tesla,

00:03:28.960 --> 00:03:31.640
pointing to where the technology could eventually lead us all

00:03:31.640 --> 00:03:33.140
if the pieces fall into place.

00:03:33.800 --> 00:03:36.380
The exact timeline remains the big open question

00:03:36.380 --> 00:03:38.340
as it always does with these kinds of visions.

00:03:39.140 --> 00:03:43.220
Even so, it serves as a reminder that the company is still thinking

00:03:43.220 --> 00:03:46.040
well beyond simply selling more vehicles in the near term.

00:03:46.480 --> 00:03:48.400
This kind of forward-looking messaging

00:03:48.400 --> 00:03:50.760
keeps the broader industry conversation moving,

00:03:50.940 --> 00:03:53.900
even when day-to-day execution hits the inevitable hurdles.

00:03:54.280 --> 00:03:55.660
I find it interesting because it shows

00:03:55.660 --> 00:03:57.860
they haven't backed away from the grander ambition

00:03:57.860 --> 00:04:01.200
even as they grind through the supervised full-self-driving phase.

00:04:01.500 --> 00:04:04.100
It's easy to get caught up in the quarterly delivery numbers

00:04:04.100 --> 00:04:05.480
or the latest software delay,

00:04:05.480 --> 00:04:07.600
but these videos are Tesla's way of saying

00:04:07.600 --> 00:04:09.880
the real price is still further down the road.

00:04:10.220 --> 00:04:12.160
Whether that creates helpful inspiration

00:04:12.160 --> 00:04:14.940
or just adds more pressure is something only time will tell.

00:04:15.580 --> 00:04:18.060
That future-focused optimism sits in contrast

00:04:18.060 --> 00:04:20.720
to some more grounded realities we're seeing right now

00:04:20.720 --> 00:04:21.600
with the cyber truck.

00:04:22.020 --> 00:04:25.160
Reports show that Musk's company's particularly SpaceX

00:04:25.160 --> 00:04:27.720
accounted for roughly one in five cyber trucks

00:04:27.720 --> 00:04:30.020
registered in the fourth quarter of 2025.

00:04:30.760 --> 00:04:32.380
Internal support of this scale

00:04:32.380 --> 00:04:35.340
makes sense in the early days when you're still ramping production

00:04:35.340 --> 00:04:36.820
and working out the kinks.

00:04:37.200 --> 00:04:40.460
But it cannot last forever if the truck is going to prove itself

00:04:40.460 --> 00:04:43.360
with regular customers outside that circle.

00:04:43.880 --> 00:04:46.960
It raises fair questions about the level of organic demand right now.

00:04:47.400 --> 00:04:50.460
Broadening appeal will likely require more than just internal volume

00:04:50.460 --> 00:04:52.240
to build real momentum in the market.

00:04:52.900 --> 00:04:55.380
This is an honest reality check on how product success

00:04:55.380 --> 00:04:57.320
ultimately gets measured over time.

00:04:57.760 --> 00:05:00.660
The cyber truck generates enormous attention wherever it goes,

00:05:00.660 --> 00:05:03.620
yet turning that attention into widespread purchases

00:05:03.620 --> 00:05:06.280
by people who don't work at one of Elon's companies

00:05:06.280 --> 00:05:07.780
is the next real test.

00:05:08.340 --> 00:05:11.280
I think it's healthy to acknowledge this without panic.

00:05:12.140 --> 00:05:14.200
Early adopters and employees have always played

00:05:14.200 --> 00:05:15.960
an outsized role in Tesla launches,

00:05:16.220 --> 00:05:18.900
but the truck's long-term success depends on whether it can cross

00:05:18.900 --> 00:05:21.060
over to contractors, families, and enthusiasts

00:05:21.060 --> 00:05:23.480
who simply want a capable electric pickup.

00:05:23.840 --> 00:05:25.780
We're still in that awkward adolescent phase

00:05:25.780 --> 00:05:27.280
where the numbers can look impressive,

00:05:27.540 --> 00:05:29.200
but the foundation needs to broaden.

00:05:29.840 --> 00:05:32.660
Speaking of product gaps, there are fresh hints

00:05:32.660 --> 00:05:35.620
that Tesla may be working on something more family-oriented.

00:05:35.920 --> 00:05:39.780
The company appears to be hinting at a new family-focused electric vehicle

00:05:39.780 --> 00:05:42.580
that could blend some of that cyber truck styling

00:05:42.580 --> 00:05:45.480
with more practical size and seating configurations.

00:05:46.040 --> 00:05:48.720
If it materializes, this would fill a noticeable gap

00:05:48.720 --> 00:05:49.720
in their current lineup.

00:05:50.040 --> 00:05:51.440
Many families like the bold look

00:05:51.440 --> 00:05:53.760
but need something better suited to everyday hauling,

00:05:53.920 --> 00:05:55.220
car seats, and passenger needs

00:05:55.220 --> 00:05:56.940
without going full three-row SUV.

00:05:57.500 --> 00:05:59.500
It makes sense from a product strategy view

00:05:59.500 --> 00:06:00.960
to round out the range this way.

00:06:01.200 --> 00:06:03.420
Right now, the lineup jumps from the Model Y

00:06:03.420 --> 00:06:05.720
to the much larger and more expensive

00:06:05.720 --> 00:06:07.300
cyber truck in certain markets,

00:06:07.560 --> 00:06:09.200
leaving some buyers stuck in the middle.

00:06:09.600 --> 00:06:11.900
A vehicle that keeps the futuristic edges

00:06:11.900 --> 00:06:13.440
but adds easier access,

00:06:14.080 --> 00:06:15.140
more interior flexibility,

00:06:15.820 --> 00:06:17.820
and perhaps a slightly smaller footprint

00:06:17.820 --> 00:06:20.620
could bring in an entirely new group of customers

00:06:20.620 --> 00:06:23.040
who have been waiting for Tesla to speak their language.

00:06:23.520 --> 00:06:25.060
I'm thoughtful about this one

00:06:25.060 --> 00:06:28.860
because product expansion has always been one of their harder challenges.

00:06:29.460 --> 00:06:31.980
Getting the pricing range and production efficiency

00:06:31.980 --> 00:06:34.400
right on a new body style is never simple

00:06:34.400 --> 00:06:37.140
but the payoff could be substantial if they land it.

00:06:37.780 --> 00:06:38.900
While we wait on that,

00:06:39.460 --> 00:06:41.260
Tesla's existing lineup is still winning

00:06:41.260 --> 00:06:43.480
in some interesting international markets.

00:06:44.000 --> 00:06:46.860
Chinese made electric vehicles are gaining real traction

00:06:46.860 --> 00:06:49.100
in South Korea's imported vehicle market

00:06:49.100 --> 00:06:51.380
and Tesla models are leading the pack there.

00:06:51.940 --> 00:06:53.700
It demonstrates that strong range,

00:06:54.020 --> 00:06:55.000
advanced technology,

00:06:55.280 --> 00:06:58.200
and brand strength can cut through geopolitical tension.

00:06:58.580 --> 00:07:00.880
This performance helps offset softer spots

00:07:00.880 --> 00:07:02.280
in other regions for the company.

00:07:02.800 --> 00:07:05.560
It also shows genuine global pull for their vehicles

00:07:05.560 --> 00:07:07.580
even in competitive Asian markets

00:07:07.580 --> 00:07:09.540
where local manufacturers are strong.

00:07:09.960 --> 00:07:11.440
Success like this reminds us

00:07:11.440 --> 00:07:13.460
that customer priorities often matter

00:07:13.460 --> 00:07:15.620
more than headlines about trade relations.

00:07:16.200 --> 00:07:18.460
South Korea has always been a discerning market

00:07:18.460 --> 00:07:20.240
that values quality and innovation.

00:07:20.240 --> 00:07:22.680
So seeing Tesla hold the top spot

00:07:22.680 --> 00:07:24.740
among imports says something meaningful

00:07:24.740 --> 00:07:26.800
about how the cars are actually perceived

00:07:26.800 --> 00:07:27.960
once people drive them.

00:07:28.440 --> 00:07:29.720
It's one of those data points

00:07:29.720 --> 00:07:32.080
that doesn't get as much attention as the big markets

00:07:32.080 --> 00:07:33.640
but probably deserves more.

00:07:34.180 --> 00:07:37.240
On the other hand, the whole industry is sounding a bit quieter lately.

00:07:37.480 --> 00:07:38.640
There is a noticeable pause

00:07:38.640 --> 00:07:40.320
and new electric vehicle reveals

00:07:40.320 --> 00:07:42.900
and future product teases across manufacturers.

00:07:43.480 --> 00:07:45.020
This includes Tesla as well.

00:07:45.200 --> 00:07:46.640
Some are calling it the Trump slump

00:07:46.640 --> 00:07:48.400
pointing to policy uncertainty

00:07:48.400 --> 00:07:50.480
and shifting political winds as the cause.

00:07:50.940 --> 00:07:52.780
For Tesla, this quiet period stands out

00:07:52.780 --> 00:07:55.060
because they have historically used announcements

00:07:55.060 --> 00:07:56.300
to maintain momentum

00:07:56.300 --> 00:07:59.140
and keep the conversation focused on their roadmap.

00:07:59.660 --> 00:08:00.780
It will be worth watching

00:08:00.780 --> 00:08:02.340
whether this is temporary caution

00:08:02.340 --> 00:08:04.600
or something more lasting in the business environment.

00:08:04.960 --> 00:08:07.220
When the entire sector slows its messaging

00:08:07.220 --> 00:08:08.040
at the same time,

00:08:08.040 --> 00:08:09.140
it can create a vacuum

00:08:09.140 --> 00:08:10.460
that makes consumers hesitate.

00:08:11.080 --> 00:08:12.960
Tesla has usually thrived in chaos

00:08:12.960 --> 00:08:14.700
by doubling down on bold claims.

00:08:15.020 --> 00:08:16.900
So seeing them take a breath here is notable.

00:08:16.900 --> 00:08:19.100
I think it reflects a more mature approach

00:08:19.100 --> 00:08:20.340
to managing expectations

00:08:20.340 --> 00:08:22.320
in a world where actual execution

00:08:22.320 --> 00:08:23.500
on manufacturing scale

00:08:23.500 --> 00:08:25.720
and regulatory approval matters more than ever.

00:08:26.060 --> 00:08:27.740
While the daily news cycle focuses

00:08:27.740 --> 00:08:28.940
on products and policy,

00:08:29.060 --> 00:08:30.560
it's worth stepping back to understand

00:08:30.560 --> 00:08:32.500
what's actually happening inside the battery cells

00:08:32.500 --> 00:08:33.620
that power all of this.

00:08:34.540 --> 00:08:37.040
Battery chemistry is one of those fundamental topics

00:08:37.040 --> 00:08:38.300
that doesn't get discussed

00:08:38.300 --> 00:08:39.980
enough outside of engineering circles.

00:08:40.400 --> 00:08:41.540
Yet the choices made here

00:08:41.540 --> 00:08:44.420
directly shape range, cost, safety, longevity

00:08:44.420 --> 00:08:46.760
and which markets a vehicle fits best.

00:08:46.760 --> 00:08:49.100
Early lithium ion batteries and cars

00:08:49.100 --> 00:08:50.240
were mostly variations

00:08:50.240 --> 00:08:52.020
of nickel manganese cobalt.

00:08:52.160 --> 00:08:54.420
This chemistry delivers strong energy density

00:08:54.420 --> 00:08:56.700
for decent range without needing an enormous pack.

00:08:57.420 --> 00:08:58.580
The tradeoff is higher cost

00:08:58.580 --> 00:09:00.360
because nickel and cobalt are expensive

00:09:00.360 --> 00:09:01.960
with volatile supply chains.

00:09:02.600 --> 00:09:04.020
Thermal stability also requires

00:09:04.020 --> 00:09:04.960
careful management

00:09:04.960 --> 00:09:06.580
to avoid overheating risks.

00:09:07.120 --> 00:09:08.300
Many Western manufacturers

00:09:08.300 --> 00:09:09.380
leaned on this approach

00:09:09.380 --> 00:09:11.400
for years to match customer expectations

00:09:11.400 --> 00:09:12.800
around performance and range.

00:09:13.300 --> 00:09:15.080
Then the industry saw a big shift

00:09:15.080 --> 00:09:17.020
toward lithium iron phosphate.

00:09:17.480 --> 00:09:19.420
This option trades some energy density

00:09:19.420 --> 00:09:20.840
for big gains in cost,

00:09:21.120 --> 00:09:22.520
safety and cycle life.

00:09:23.040 --> 00:09:23.800
It runs cooler,

00:09:24.080 --> 00:09:26.500
resists degradation over thousands of charges

00:09:26.500 --> 00:09:28.100
and uses abundant materials

00:09:28.100 --> 00:09:29.280
that are easier to source.

00:09:29.820 --> 00:09:31.600
China embraced this chemistry early

00:09:31.600 --> 00:09:32.820
because it fit their focus

00:09:32.820 --> 00:09:34.580
on affordable urban mobility

00:09:34.580 --> 00:09:35.900
and local supply chains.

00:09:36.340 --> 00:09:37.420
Their makers could deliver

00:09:37.420 --> 00:09:39.300
reliable range for daily use

00:09:39.300 --> 00:09:41.200
at prices that undercut competitors.

00:09:41.740 --> 00:09:43.400
The perspective there is pragmatic,

00:09:43.400 --> 00:09:45.540
emphasizing total cost of ownership

00:09:45.540 --> 00:09:47.140
over chasing maximum range

00:09:47.140 --> 00:09:48.420
on every single vehicle.

00:09:49.220 --> 00:09:50.480
Tesla took its own path

00:09:50.480 --> 00:09:53.260
by pushing the 4680 cell format.

00:09:53.820 --> 00:09:55.280
These larger cells reduce

00:09:55.280 --> 00:09:56.760
manufacturing complexity

00:09:56.760 --> 00:09:58.200
and improve energy flow.

00:09:58.660 --> 00:10:00.760
They also allow structural integration

00:10:00.760 --> 00:10:02.040
into the vehicle itself.

00:10:02.680 --> 00:10:03.980
This is classic Tesla

00:10:03.980 --> 00:10:06.160
solving problems at the full system level

00:10:06.160 --> 00:10:07.980
instead of accepting old trade-offs.

00:10:08.600 --> 00:10:09.600
The chemistry inside

00:10:09.600 --> 00:10:11.420
has varied with high nickel experiments

00:10:11.420 --> 00:10:13.540
and blends that cut cobalt use.

00:10:14.060 --> 00:10:15.620
The aim is to improve both cost

00:10:15.620 --> 00:10:17.480
and vehicle dynamics simultaneously.

00:10:18.000 --> 00:10:20.000
Different regions reflect different priorities

00:10:20.000 --> 00:10:20.860
in these choices.

00:10:21.620 --> 00:10:23.440
Europe often faces more regulatory

00:10:23.440 --> 00:10:25.220
pressure on supply chain ethics

00:10:25.220 --> 00:10:26.300
and carbon footprints.

00:10:27.220 --> 00:10:28.400
American efforts have sometimes

00:10:28.400 --> 00:10:29.700
emphasized high performance

00:10:29.700 --> 00:10:31.240
for trucks and longer range needs.

00:10:31.820 --> 00:10:33.860
China proved that lithium iron phosphate

00:10:33.860 --> 00:10:35.440
can dominate volume segments

00:10:35.440 --> 00:10:37.120
when scaled with local advantages.

00:10:37.960 --> 00:10:39.240
The first principles insight

00:10:39.240 --> 00:10:41.020
is that no single chemistry wins

00:10:41.020 --> 00:10:41.640
everywhere.

00:10:42.060 --> 00:10:43.020
Range matters less

00:10:43.020 --> 00:10:45.380
if the battery lasts twice as many cycles.

00:10:46.020 --> 00:10:46.900
Cost matters more

00:10:46.900 --> 00:10:48.300
in price-sensitive markets

00:10:48.300 --> 00:10:49.780
while longevity becomes key

00:10:49.780 --> 00:10:51.120
to proving electric vehicles

00:10:51.120 --> 00:10:52.580
can outlast gas ones.

00:10:53.400 --> 00:10:55.400
Tesla's 4680 approach

00:10:55.400 --> 00:10:56.580
tries to thread the needle

00:10:56.580 --> 00:10:57.340
through format

00:10:57.340 --> 00:10:58.660
and production innovation

00:10:58.660 --> 00:11:00.980
rather than just picking one existing recipe.

00:11:01.720 --> 00:11:03.000
The winners going forward

00:11:03.000 --> 00:11:03.940
will likely be those

00:11:03.940 --> 00:11:04.860
who treat chemistry

00:11:04.860 --> 00:11:06.020
as a practical tool

00:11:06.020 --> 00:11:07.740
matched to real customer needs

00:11:07.740 --> 00:11:09.260
rather than a marketing story.

00:11:09.800 --> 00:11:11.440
It's easy to get lost in the hype

00:11:11.440 --> 00:11:12.940
around any particular breakthrough

00:11:12.940 --> 00:11:14.540
but the truth is the right battery

00:11:14.540 --> 00:11:15.600
is the one that makes the whole

00:11:15.600 --> 00:11:16.580
vehicle work better

00:11:16.580 --> 00:11:18.780
for the people who actually drive it every day.

00:11:19.180 --> 00:11:20.740
If you're relatively new to Tesla

00:11:20.740 --> 00:11:22.200
or just starting to pay attention

00:11:22.200 --> 00:11:23.040
as an investor,

00:11:23.560 --> 00:11:25.320
the full self-driving conversation

00:11:25.320 --> 00:11:26.380
can feel overwhelming.

00:11:26.820 --> 00:11:28.320
There is talk of neural nets,

00:11:28.660 --> 00:11:29.580
occupancy networks,

00:11:30.060 --> 00:11:30.880
end-to-end learning

00:11:30.880 --> 00:11:32.240
and endless comparisons

00:11:32.240 --> 00:11:33.220
to other companies.

00:11:33.500 --> 00:11:34.320
Let me cut through that

00:11:34.320 --> 00:11:35.840
and explain it clearly

00:11:35.840 --> 00:11:37.720
the way a friend would over coffee.

00:11:38.460 --> 00:11:40.340
Early autopilot hardware

00:11:40.340 --> 00:11:42.420
like HW2 used cameras

00:11:42.420 --> 00:11:43.180
and computers

00:11:43.180 --> 00:11:44.360
for basic lane-keeping

00:11:44.360 --> 00:11:45.980
and adaptive cruise control.

00:11:46.320 --> 00:11:47.140
It was helpful

00:11:47.140 --> 00:11:48.420
but limited in scope.

00:11:49.100 --> 00:11:50.560
HW3 brought real

00:11:50.560 --> 00:11:51.900
neural network capability

00:11:51.900 --> 00:11:53.040
so the car could interpret

00:11:53.040 --> 00:11:53.880
camera images

00:11:53.880 --> 00:11:55.140
with artificial intelligence

00:11:55.140 --> 00:11:56.600
instead of hand-coded rules.

00:11:57.320 --> 00:11:58.960
HW4 improved the cameras,

00:11:59.460 --> 00:12:00.280
processing power

00:12:00.280 --> 00:12:01.040
and redundancy

00:12:01.040 --> 00:12:02.020
for better performance

00:12:02.020 --> 00:12:02.940
in tough conditions

00:12:02.940 --> 00:12:03.620
like fog,

00:12:04.060 --> 00:12:04.540
heavy rain,

00:12:04.840 --> 00:12:05.460
or bright sun.

00:12:06.100 --> 00:12:06.980
One of the biggest shifts

00:12:06.980 --> 00:12:07.820
was going vision

00:12:07.820 --> 00:12:09.480
only by removing radar.

00:12:09.980 --> 00:12:11.080
Tesla argued that humans

00:12:11.080 --> 00:12:12.540
drive mostly with vision

00:12:12.540 --> 00:12:14.420
so a well-trained neural network

00:12:14.420 --> 00:12:15.700
should be able to as well.

00:12:16.300 --> 00:12:17.820
Radar sometimes created

00:12:17.820 --> 00:12:18.640
false positives,

00:12:18.780 --> 00:12:19.580
especially in rain

00:12:19.580 --> 00:12:21.080
or when sensors got dirty.

00:12:21.880 --> 00:12:22.840
So far, the data

00:12:22.840 --> 00:12:24.300
from their supervised systems

00:12:24.300 --> 00:12:25.920
suggests this bet is paying off

00:12:25.920 --> 00:12:27.340
even if it has taken longer

00:12:27.340 --> 00:12:28.420
than many expected.

00:12:29.240 --> 00:12:30.220
Two key concepts

00:12:30.220 --> 00:12:31.080
worth understanding

00:12:31.080 --> 00:12:32.540
are the occupancy network

00:12:32.540 --> 00:12:34.140
and transformer-based planning.

00:12:34.680 --> 00:12:35.800
The occupancy network

00:12:35.800 --> 00:12:36.640
builds a living

00:12:36.640 --> 00:12:37.920
three-dimensional model

00:12:37.920 --> 00:12:39.480
of the world around the car.

00:12:39.980 --> 00:12:41.780
It understands occupied spaces

00:12:41.780 --> 00:12:43.600
and how they might change over time.

00:12:44.360 --> 00:12:45.720
The transformer architecture,

00:12:46.000 --> 00:12:47.780
similar to what powers chat tools,

00:12:48.040 --> 00:12:48.800
handles prediction

00:12:48.800 --> 00:12:50.840
and decides the safest path forward.

00:12:51.420 --> 00:12:52.560
This end-to-end approach

00:12:52.560 --> 00:12:53.380
learns directly

00:12:53.380 --> 00:12:54.920
from real driving examples

00:12:54.920 --> 00:12:56.140
instead of long lists

00:12:56.140 --> 00:12:57.280
of if-then rules

00:12:57.280 --> 00:12:59.200
that engineers have to write manually.

00:12:59.800 --> 00:13:01.040
Other companies like Waymo

00:13:01.040 --> 00:13:02.500
and Crews take a different route

00:13:02.500 --> 00:13:03.560
with LiDAR for precise

00:13:03.560 --> 00:13:05.440
3D point clouds plus radar

00:13:05.440 --> 00:13:06.040
and cameras.

00:13:06.560 --> 00:13:07.840
Their systems often work

00:13:07.840 --> 00:13:09.020
in limited mapped areas

00:13:09.020 --> 00:13:10.600
with remote human supervision

00:13:10.600 --> 00:13:11.780
available when needed.

00:13:12.340 --> 00:13:13.980
Tesla bets that vision scales better

00:13:13.980 --> 00:13:15.200
because cameras are inexpensive

00:13:15.200 --> 00:13:17.020
and the fleet generates huge amounts

00:13:17.020 --> 00:13:18.480
of real-world data daily.

00:13:19.060 --> 00:13:19.840
The goal is good enough

00:13:19.840 --> 00:13:20.900
sensing that improves

00:13:20.900 --> 00:13:22.140
through software across

00:13:22.140 --> 00:13:23.560
millions of vehicles worldwide

00:13:23.560 --> 00:13:24.720
instead of perfect sensing

00:13:24.720 --> 00:13:25.860
in just a few cities.

00:13:26.400 --> 00:13:27.840
For new owners or investors,

00:13:28.080 --> 00:13:28.920
the key is understanding

00:13:28.920 --> 00:13:30.340
the long-term scaling curve.

00:13:30.860 --> 00:13:31.880
Tesla still operates

00:13:31.880 --> 00:13:32.840
in supervised mode

00:13:32.840 --> 00:13:33.520
in most places

00:13:33.520 --> 00:13:35.060
so drivers must stay attentive.

00:13:35.440 --> 00:13:37.060
The push toward unsupervised

00:13:37.060 --> 00:13:39.100
continues but real-world edge cases

00:13:39.100 --> 00:13:40.420
and regulators keep timelines

00:13:40.420 --> 00:13:40.920
uncertain.

00:13:41.500 --> 00:13:42.680
Waymo has shown driverless

00:13:42.680 --> 00:13:44.100
operation in select cities

00:13:44.100 --> 00:13:45.240
which proves their hardware

00:13:45.240 --> 00:13:47.220
heavy approach works in those spots.

00:13:47.640 --> 00:13:49.220
Yet it comes at high cost

00:13:49.220 --> 00:13:50.660
and limited scale for now.

00:13:51.280 --> 00:13:52.160
Tesla's bet is

00:13:52.160 --> 00:13:53.800
that software and fleet data

00:13:53.800 --> 00:13:55.200
can solve what others address

00:13:55.200 --> 00:13:56.520
with more expensive sensors.

00:13:57.240 --> 00:13:58.400
This is why every update

00:13:58.400 --> 00:13:59.220
feels meaningful

00:13:59.220 --> 00:14:00.760
because older cars can

00:14:00.760 --> 00:14:01.700
improve meaningfully

00:14:01.700 --> 00:14:02.340
through the air.

00:14:02.740 --> 00:14:04.040
The architecture is elegant

00:14:04.040 --> 00:14:04.860
in its simplicity

00:14:04.860 --> 00:14:06.280
but teaching it to handle

00:14:06.280 --> 00:14:07.760
every unusual situation

00:14:07.760 --> 00:14:08.460
takes time,

00:14:08.880 --> 00:14:10.300
miles, and steady iteration.

00:14:10.780 --> 00:14:12.040
Patience is still required

00:14:12.040 --> 00:14:12.900
on the path ahead.

00:14:13.480 --> 00:14:14.260
What I appreciate

00:14:14.260 --> 00:14:15.620
about this approach is how it

00:14:15.620 --> 00:14:16.480
bets on the collective

00:14:16.480 --> 00:14:17.860
learning of the entire fleet

00:14:17.860 --> 00:14:19.020
instead of trying

00:14:19.020 --> 00:14:20.720
to engineer perfection in a lab

00:14:20.720 --> 00:14:22.100
that doesn't make it easy

00:14:22.100 --> 00:14:22.940
but it feels like

00:14:22.940 --> 00:14:24.380
the only way to eventually

00:14:24.380 --> 00:14:26.060
reach the scale they're aiming for.

00:14:26.680 --> 00:14:27.920
Before we go keep an eye

00:14:27.920 --> 00:14:29.180
on how those free trials

00:14:29.180 --> 00:14:30.180
of full self-driving

00:14:30.180 --> 00:14:31.620
supervised land in the Netherlands

00:14:31.620 --> 00:14:33.240
because that real-world feedback

00:14:33.240 --> 00:14:34.740
could shape the next wave

00:14:34.740 --> 00:14:36.560
of refinements in meaningful ways.

